# Dragon's Rage Channeler: "Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, surveil 1". Casting an Ornithopter (a creature spell) asks
# nothing (! Bot1.Arrange) and neither does Bot2's Lightning Bolt (not Bot1's spell); Bot1's own Chain Lightning does, and
# Bot1 keeps the Mountain on top (the other branch of "you may put it into your graveyard"), then lets a second Mountain
# go. Delirium needs four types: with an instant, a sorcery and a land in the graveyard (three) the Channeler is still a 1/1
# without flying.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Dragon's Rage Channeler
Mountain
Ornithopter
Chain Lightning
Lightning Bolt
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dragon's Rage Channeler.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
! Bot1.Arrange
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#1.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Chain Lightning.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Arrange(Mountain |)
